<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nouakchott</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Nouakchott is the capital and largest city of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mauritania">Mauritania</a>, near the Atlantic coast. The French colony had been governed from Saint-Louis in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/senegal">Senegal</a>, so from 1957 a new capital was built on the site of a small village for the soon-to-be independent country, planned for about 15,000 people. Drought and migration from the desert have since swelled it to more than a million inhabitants.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/nouakchott.jpg" alt="Nouakchott" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Laminesall96 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nouakchott.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
